course: dictionary
lesson: 10362
title: Trauma: a deep hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trauma is a noun, and it has three main meanings. The clues in the sentences around it show you which one is meant. «Trauma is a very deep hurt from something terrifying; it can last a long time, it is not weakness.» Terrifying and a long time tell you this is about the mind and feelings.
explain: In medicine, trauma means a serious injury to the body, like one from an accident. Hospitals have a «trauma unit» to treat it. The clue is the place: a hospital treats injuries to the body.
explain: Sometimes people use trauma as a joke about a small problem. Ask yourself: is this really frightening? If not, the speaker is probably joking. Real trauma is never a joke, so always think about how serious the situation is.
fact: Trauma means a very upsetting or frightening experience that can hurt someone's mind and feelings for a long time.
fact: «Emotional trauma» is hurt to the mind and feelings, and «head trauma» is a serious injury to the head.
fact: People who go through trauma, such as accidents, disasters or war, may need help and kindness.
fact: Talking to a trusted adult or a counsellor can help, and needing help is not a sign of weakness.
fact: Flashbacks are sudden, vivid memories of something frightening, and there is no time limit for getting over trauma.
exercise: «Trauma is the lasting effect of something very frightening.» What does trauma mean here? | A happy surprise party | *A very upsetting experience that hurts the mind for a long time | A short sleep after lunch | A football match
exercise: «The hospital has a trauma unit for people with serious injuries.» What does trauma mean here? | A school trip | A bad mood for one afternoon | A kind of sweet | *A serious injury to the body
exercise: Sam says, «Losing my pencil was such a trauma!» Why is Sam probably joking? | Pencils are always dangerous | *A lost pencil is a small problem, not a frightening experience | Sam is a doctor | Sam has never lost anything before
test: What is the best way to get help after a frightening experience? | Pretend nothing happened and hope it fades | Keep it secret and never speak about it | Wait for a joke to make you feel better | *Talk to a trusted adult or a counsellor
test: Which sentence uses trauma in its serious, medical sense? | «I had a trauma when I dropped my crisps.» | «Our class had a trauma about the lunch menu.» | *«He was taken to the trauma unit after the crash.» | «Trauma is my favourite word this week.»
exam: Which statement about trauma is true? | Trauma only happens to adults | Trauma is only a joke word | Trauma always disappears in one day | *Trauma is not a sign of weakness, and help from a counsellor can make it lighter
